WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.711
Welcome to the Accurex Dynamic Form code tour.

2
00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:03.890
This is episode one.

3
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.131
By the end of it, you will know what this project does,

4
00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:10.196
how to run it, and what happens when the page loads.

5
00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:12.700
Here is the idea in one sentence.

6
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.310
Business users design a form in the CRM.

7
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.529
The CRM sends that design as JSON.

8
00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:21.705
And this code turns the JSON into a working form on the website.

9
00:00:21.705 --> 00:00:23.662
Nobody writes HTML for a form.

10
00:00:24.015 --> 00:00:26.573
Our example is the Accurex Start-Up Report.

11
00:00:26.573 --> 00:00:31.451
Technicians fill it in on site when they commission kitchen ventilation equipment:

12
00:00:31.451 --> 00:00:34.902
control panels, hoods, exhaust fans and make-up air units.

13
00:00:35.254 --> 00:00:38.553
This whole page was drawn from one JSON file.

14
00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:41.999
The header shows the job and the report status.

15
00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:46.619
Each piece of equipment gets a tab: CP-1, HD-1, EF-1 and MUA-1.

16
00:00:46.971 --> 00:00:48.679
Let’s answer a question.

17
00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:51.383
On the control panel: power to lights?

18
00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:51.596
No.

19
00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:53.102
Watch what happens.

20
00:00:53.102 --> 00:00:54.560
The question is flagged.

21
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.382
The section counter turns red.

22
00:00:56.382 --> 00:00:58.022
And the tab gets a red dot.

23
00:00:58.374 --> 00:01:01.504
Every problem is also listed in one place, near the top,

24
00:01:01.504 --> 00:01:04.187
with a View link that jumps straight back to it.

25
00:01:04.538 --> 00:01:05.936
Now a measured reading.

26
00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:11.465
The nameplate says eighteen point two amps, and the overload is set to nineteen point five.

27
00:01:11.465 --> 00:01:14.564
That is seven percent off, so the form says: check.

28
00:01:14.915 --> 00:01:22.394
To run it yourself, clone the repository and start the development server: python3 dev-server.

29
00:01:22.394 --> 00:01:22.633
py.

30
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.985
Then open sample.

31
00:01:23.985 --> 00:01:26.293
html on localhost, port 8080.

32
00:01:26.644 --> 00:01:29.522
There is no npm, no build step and no framework.

33
00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.819
The browser runs the files exactly as they are written.

34
00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.544
There are three layers.

35
00:01:34.544 --> 00:01:36.634
The configuration says what to ask.

36
00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:39.500
The framework, in the src folder, does the work.

37
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.248
And the host page says where to draw the form.

38
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.524
When the page loads, render downloads the JSON, builds every block of the page,

39
00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:52.261
puts back any saved draft, and calls refresh, which draws the current state.

40
00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.164
In the next episode, we open the folders,

41
00:01:55.164 --> 00:02:00.144
and meet the one loop that explains the whole codebase: set value, then refresh.
